From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] rpcrt4: RpcSs/RpcSm memory management and the NDR helpers using it

RpcSsAllocate/Free/EnableAllocate/DisableAllocate/GetThreadHandle/SetThreadHandle/SetClientAllocFree/SwapClientAllocFree, their RpcSm variants, NdrRpcSsEnableAllocate/DisableAllocate/DefaultAllocate/DefaultFree, NdrRpcSmClientAllocate/ClientFree and NdrRpcSmSetClientToOsf (defined but not exported) were spec stubs. New rpc_ss.c: a thread's memory environment (shareable through RpcSsSetThreadHandle), freed block by block or all at once, and the per-thread client allocator. Synchronous server stubs of [enable_allocate] procedures run the manager routine in an environment, freed when the call ends; client stubs allocate such out parameters with the client allocator. rpcndr.h gains the declarations.
---
--- a/dlls/rpcrt4/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/rpcrt4/Makefile.in
@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@
 	rpc_epmap.c \
 	rpc_message.c \
 	rpc_server.c \
+	rpc_ss.c \
 	rpc_transport.c \
 	rpcrt4_main.c \
 	thunks.c \
--- a/dlls/rpcrt4/ndr_stubless.c
+++ b/dlls/rpcrt4/ndr_stubless.c
